From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: take AKM suites from the BSSes, not from the radio

The AKM Suite Capabilities TLV (0xCC) went out empty, so no peer could learn
what security this device speaks - and a backhaul link is negotiated from
exactly that. EasyMesh 6.1 section 5.2.3 requires an SAE-capable bSTA to be
able to associate; with an empty TLV there is nothing to agree on.

The generator was never at fault. agent_gen_akm_suite_cap() is complete and is
called; it simply had nothing to publish, because both of its sources are
empty. Measured 2026-09-01 on a live node:

  - the HAL reports none:
      ubus call wifi.radio.radioN status  ->  "ap_akms": [], "sta_akms": []
    on all three radios.

  - the fallback, agent_radio_init_default_akm_suite(), read encryption from
    the *radio* config section. Those sections carry no encryption option at
    all: /etc/config/mapagent holds twelve of them and every one is in an ap
    section, none in a radio section. So enc was always 0 and
    default_akm_suites_from_encryption() correctly returned zero suites.

Encryption is a property of a BSS, not of a radio, which is why it lives in
the ap sections and why the radio sections never grew one. Read it from there.

Every AP on the radio is merged, because one radio can host BSSes with
different security and the TLV advertises what the *device* can do: a
fronthaul on sae-mixed and a backhaul on sae must both be visible, or a peer
speaking only one of them concludes we cannot talk to it at all.

Reading it from the running configuration also means existing nodes pick it up
on their next start. A fix in the config generator would not have reached
them - those sections are written once and sysupgrade keeps them.

--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -3906,8 +3906,23 @@
 static void agent_radio_init_default_akm_suite(struct agent *a,
 					       struct wifi_radio_element *re)
 {
-	struct agent_config_radio *rcfg = get_agent_config_radio(&a->cfg, re->name);
-	uint16_t enc = rcfg ? rcfg->encryption : 0;
+	struct netif_apcfg *apcfg;
+	uint16_t enc = 0;
+
+	/* Encryption is a property of the BSS, not of the radio. The radio
+	 * sections carry no encryption option at all - every one of them
+	 * lives in an ap section - so reading it from the radio yielded 0 and
+	 * the AKM Suite Capabilities TLV went out empty, leaving no peer able
+	 * to learn what security this device speaks.
+	 *
+	 * Merge every AP on this radio: one radio can host BSSes with
+	 * different security, and the TLV advertises what the device can do.
+	 */
+	list_for_each_entry(apcfg, &a->cfg.aplist, list) {
+		if (strncmp(apcfg->device, re->name, sizeof(apcfg->device)))
+			continue;
+		enc |= get_encryption(apcfg->encryption);
+	}
 
 	re->num_ap_akms = default_akm_suites_from_encryption(enc,
 			(uint8_t *)re->ap_akms, MAX_AKM_SUITES);
